{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue, net interest income plus noninterest income, grew from $21.0 billion in FY2016 to $28.5 billion in FY2025, a 3.5% CAGR [D5][D219]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was not smooth: revenue was flat at $22.7 billion in FY2021, then jumped 15.8% in FY2023 to $28.0 billion [D117][D169][D189]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 step change came from higher rates on earning assets and the MUB acquisition, which lifted net interest income 18.1% [D184][P33]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2024 reversed 2.4% as higher rates on deposit mix and pricing cut net interest income 6.4% [D214][D209][P21]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "FY2025 recovered 4.4% on loan growth, fixed asset repricing and lower deposit rates [D239][P16]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Payment Services was the steadiest engine, growing 5.4% in FY2025 to $7.4 billion, 25.8% of revenue and +1.4pp of growth [S61][D259][D260][D261]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "That segment's net revenue rose on higher average loan balances and lower funding costs, plus merchant processing and card revenue from higher sales volume [P4]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Consumer and Business Banking shrank 3.9% in FY2025, subtracting 1.3pp, as deposit mix and second-quarter loan sales cut net interest income [D252][D253][P6]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Noninterest income outgrew net interest income in FY2025, 7.6% against 2.2%, lifting its share of revenue [D235][D234]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net income grew 20.2% against 4.4% revenue growth, so costs fell faster than revenue [D227][D239]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The efficiency ratio was 59.0% in FY2025, just below its 59.3% window median and far under the 67.4% FY2023 high [D220][D277][D276]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "It ranks at the 14th percentile of seven banks peers, better than the 61.7% peer median [D280][D281]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Noninterest expense fell 2.0% in FY2025 on prior-year merger and FDIC charges and lower compensation, partly offset by technology and marketing spend [D238][P10]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2023 efficiency spike to 67.4% came from merger and integration charges, the $734 million FDIC special assessment and MUB operating costs [D170][P30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 tax rate of 20.2% left net margin at 26.5%, close to operating profitability [D215][D223]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating cash flow is not a meaningful earnings-quality measure for a bank; capital return is the better test [F60][F30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $8.0 billion was 1.05x net income in FY2025, against a 1.24x FY2021 reading [F60][F30][D216][D114]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends of $3.7 billion were 48.3% of FY2025 net income, up from $2.8 billion in FY2022 [D218][F30][D142]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Stock-based compensation was $235 million, 2.9% of operating cash flow [X37][D217]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity was 12.2% in FY2025, above the 11.8% peer median and at the 71st percentile of seven banks [D226][D283][D282]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Loans were 73.5% of deposits, up from 67.2% in FY2021 as deposit growth outran lending [D224][D122]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The allowance was 2.0% of loans, and the credit-loss provision was 7.7% of revenue, at the 50th percentile of four peers against a 6.1% median [D225][D221][D284][D285]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Shareholders' equity rose 11.3% to $65.2 billion in FY2025 while the diluted share count fell 0.2% [D233][F114][D237]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Long-term debt is not reported after FY2022, so leverage after that year cannot be tracked from the filings [X172][R2]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Long-term debt stops being reported after FY2022 at $39.8 billion, a data break that blocks any post-2022 leverage comparison [X172][R2]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue fell 2.4% in FY2024 as deposit repricing cut net interest income 6.4%, the one down year in the window [D214][D209][R1]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The provision stayed near 8% of revenue for four years, well above the 6.3% FY2016 level, so credit costs have not normalized [D221][D7]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "If the efficiency ratio rises back above the 59.3% window median, the FY2025 cost improvement has reversed; it will show in the FY2026 10-K [D277][D220]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "A net interest income decline below the FY2025 $16.6 billion level would signal deposit repricing is again outrunning asset yields [F10][P15]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Watch whether the provision falls below the 7.7% of revenue FY2025 level, which would confirm the improved credit quality cited for the latest decline [D221][P12]."}
  ]}
]}
